    <div class="caps"><p style="animation:ladder-c0 var(--dur) linear infinite" set:html={'One level deep, <code>docker run --gpus all</code> works: <b>level 50</b>.'} /><p style="animation:ladder-c1 var(--dur) linear infinite" set:html={'Inside a Docker-in-Docker daemon, <code>--gpus</code> fails: the inner daemon has no NVIDIA runtime of its own.'} /><p style="animation:ladder-c2 var(--dur) linear infinite" set:html={"Passing the mounts to the inner container doesn't help. <code>--gpus</code> gave the outer one individual files, not the folders, so there is nothing to pass down: <b>exit 127</b>."} /><p style="animation:ladder-c3 var(--dur) linear infinite" set:html={'By hand instead: <code>/dev/dxg</code>, <code>/usr/lib/wsl/lib</code> and <code>/usr/lib/wsl/drivers</code>, with the loader path set. <b>Level 50</b>, with no NVIDIA toolkit anywhere.'} /><p style="animation:ladder-c4 var(--dur) linear infinite" set:html={'Passed down again, the same three work one level deeper. <b>Level 50</b> at every depth I tried.'} /><p style="animation:ladder-c5 var(--dur) linear infinite" set:html={"<b>The GPU survives nesting; <code>--gpus</code> doesn't.</b> So every cluster whose nodes are containers fails stock, and can be fixed with mounts."} /></div>
